Figure 7.15 shows the emission duration time, \(\Delta\tau\) as a function of the number of participants extracted from the blast wave fit to pion HBT parameters and spectra described above. \(\Delta\tau\) increases with increasing centrality up to \(\sim\) 3 fm/c. As for the proper time, the emission duration is very small for all centralities, however it has increased with respect to the values extracted from our analysis at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}\) = 130 GeV [82] due to the improved procedure of taking Coulomb interaction into account and the consequently increase in \(R_{o}\).

